    "created_at": "2021-05-05T23:38:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-05T23:38:24Z",
    "body": "[Chromium codesearch](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/v8_binding_for_core.h;l=418;drc=f9ebf0deab3efad7c0db6843af187bb36f0ccb4c;bpv=1;bpt=1?q=IncumbentDOMWindow&ss=chromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc) indicates incumbent is used for:\r\n\r\n- `Location`\r\n- `postMessage()`\r\n- `window.close()`\r\n- `window.open()` (some uses not on the above list, although some are part of navigation)\r\n- `window.focus()` (not on the above list!!)\r\n- COOP reporting\r\n\r\nMost suspiciously the incumbentNavigationOrigin which the spec uses (see #6514) does not appear very prominently in Chromium's codebase, certainly not in the navigation stack. Instead a couple of navigation call sites (`Location` and `window.open()`) use it. Hmm.",
